<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-Feb oil products demand edges higher.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-Feb oil products demand edges higher.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's petroleum products demand rose to 136.5 million barrels in the first two months of 1997 from 135.9 million barrels a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Friday.</p>
<p>A ministry statement blamed economic slowdown, high oil product prices and energy conservation programme for the weak demand growth.</p>
<p>It said the oil refiners produced 149.4 million barrels of petroleum products in the first two months against 110.8 million a year-earlier period.</p>
<p>Production increased with Hyundai Oil Refinery Co's new 200,000 barrels-per-day (bpd) refining capacity, Yukong Ltd's 200,000 bpd and LG-Caltex Oil Corp's 220,000 bpd.</p>
<p>South Korea currently has a refining capacity of 2.44 million bpd.  </p>
<p>Oil products demand (in million barrels)</p>
<p>				    Jan-Feb '97   Jan-Feb '96</p>
<p>     TOTAL			  136.5	    135.9</p>
<p>MAJOR PRODUCTS</p>
<p>     gasoline		     10.1		9.7</p>
<p>     kerosene		     23.0	     21.1</p>
<p>     diesel			 29.5	     33.4</p>
<p>     C-type fuel oil	    30.5	     29.2</p>
<p>     naphtha			24.9	     23.9</p>
<p>     LPG			    13.9	     14.0</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
